2026-10-20 03:50 Implemented on branch k4-k8, commit 3ccb1a4.

- request() croaks with "HTTP request failed: <status line>: <error texts>" - the texts are the "error" array of the body joined with "; ", the status line is kept.
- Response::error returns an empty list for a body without an "error" key (it warned before) and does not die on an empty body.
- wait_for_delete and wait_for_pending_action take timeout (default 300 s) and interval (default 10 s) and croak when the timeout is reached.
- Only 404 and the expected 400 end the wait normally; 401, 429, a network error and every other status is rethrown - the old code polled on forever.
- The status is read from last_response->code, not from the die message: the enriched message can contain "404"/"400" inside an API error text, the old regex would have matched that.
- An undefined pendingActionId counts as "no pending action" (the old comparison warned about it).

Decisions I took:
- The wording of the card is ambiguous ("stop on errors that are not still there" vs "only 404 resp. the expected 400 may keep polling"). I kept the semantics of the old code: 404/400 end the wait, everything else aborts with the original error.
- Added the optional interval argument next to timeout - without it the polling loop cannot be tested without a 10 second sleep.
- Both wait methods return true when the wait ended as expected.

